    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever felt so energetic or worked so intensely that you were unable to function at your job or had to be hospitalized because of it?",
      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Well, um... I wouldn't say I was unable to function, exactly. It's just that, well, sometimes my enthusiasm gets a little ahead of the practicalities? Like, there was this one server migration at work that... didn't go quite as planned. I was just trying to get it done faster, you know? But it caused some issues, and they ended up putting me on administrative leave for a bit. Just to let things cool down, I think. I hope that makes sense?\n\nAnd at home... well, my wife has had to help me manage things a little more lately. Like, she's had to kind of step in with our finances because I got a bit carried away buying equipment for the home network. And she reminds me to stop working so late, which is good of her. We do end up arguing sometimes when I'm just so focused on my ideas and she wants me to slow down... I really don't mean to be difficult, I just get so wrapped up in it. \n\nI guess I've also sort of stepped back from some other things, too. I used to be really involved with the music at our church, and I liked rock climbing and mentoring junior staff, but... I just haven't been able to be as reliable with those lately. I keep meaning to show up, but my mind is just on all these other projects. Is that the kind of thing you were asking about? I want to make sure I'm giving you the right information.",
